<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What electron-packager merges into the app's Info.plist on a Mac
  (build-mac.sh, the packager's extend-info option; SPEC-mac R17). The bundle's name, identifier
  and icon come from the packager's own flags, so this holds only what has no
  flag.

  LSMinimumSystemVersion is Electron's own floor at the pinned Electron 44
  (macOS 13), deliberately below the app's floor of macOS 14 (R6, P243): a
  Mac on macOS 13 starts the app, which says its own sentence and quits, and
  only macOS 12, which Electron 44 cannot run on, gets macOS's own refusal.
  tests/test_build.py pins it. The three usage strings are the
  sentences macOS shows under its own question, once, when the app first reads a clients folder that
  sits in the Desktop, Documents or Downloads folder; each says what the
  Console does there and nothing it does not do (it never sends anything).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key>
  <string>13.0</string>
  <key>NSDesktopFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>It sorts the tax documents in the clients folder you chose, which is on your Desktop.</string>
  <key>NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>It sorts the tax documents in the clients folder you chose, which is in your Documents folder.</string>
  <key>NSDownloadsFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>It sorts the tax documents in the clients folder you chose, which is in your Downloads folder.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
